

-----------------------------------------------------------
README for Performance Script
-----------------------------------------------------------

1.Login  to performance dedicated system psky1035
==>ssh psky1035
2.Run newgrp command in the termainal
==>newgrp virtuoso.catdm
3.source ICMANAGE environment
==>source /user/virtuoso.mem/ICM/client/icmanage.cshrc
4.To run performance test user MUST cd into the perf directory. THIS is must because library are managed by  icmanage under this location.
==>/user/virtuoso.catdm/USERS/CAT_DM/perfTest

5.All setup are done and NOW you can proceed to trigger the performance RUN. Pls note do not remove or update any files under perfTest directory.

6.Run Perf by typing the following with MUST and Optional inputs for main.pl
syntax >>> ./main.pl  -lib "LIB1 LIB2 ..." -cell "cell1 cell2..." -version IC251_ISR5-023_CAT -genOnly 0

Must Arguments 
--------------
-lib  ( specify library within quote with space if more then 1 library is required)
-cell  ( specify cell within quote with space if more then 1 cell is required. Pls note then -lib and -cell need to be in the same sequence for pairing)
-version  ( specify the version dir name IC251_ISR5-023_CAT that is under installed path /user/virtuoso.cat/TOOL/IC* )
-genOnly 0 or 1 (   0 to run performance  and 1 is only to generate replay files for testing or debugging. Replay files will be created under folder code/replay )

Optional Arguments
------------------
-mode (if mode is not speccified all 7 modes( checkHier renameRefLib changeRefLib replace deleteAllMarker copyHierToEmpty copyHierToNonEmpty) will be run. If user wants to run 1 OR more modes, user can specify modes in quotes with space eg -mode "replace renameRefLib"

-manage ( if manage is not specified both modes (managed unmanaged) will be run. If user wants to run 1, user can specify as -manage managed or -manage unmanaged. If user wants to run both in any user desired order spceify in quotes -manage "unmanaged managed"


eg:-
./main.pl -lib "BM01 BM02 BM03" -cell "VP_FULLCHIP FULLCHIP XE_FULLCHIP_BASE" -version IC251_ISR5-023_CAT  -genOnly 0
./main.pl -lib "BM01 BM02 BM03" -cell "VP_FULLCHIP FULLCHIP XE_FULLCHIP_BASE" -version IC251_ISR5-023_CAT  -mode renameRefLib -genOnly 0
./main.pl -lib "BM01 BM02 BM03" -cell "VP_FULLCHIP FULLCHIP XE_FULLCHIP_BASE" -version IC251_ISR5-023_CAT  -mode "replace renameRefLib" -genOnly 0
./main.pl -lib "BM01 BM02 BM03" -cell "VP_FULLCHIP FULLCHIP XE_FULLCHIP_BASE" -version IC251_ISR5-023_CAT  -mode "replace renameRefLib" -manage managed -genOnly 0
./main.pl -lib "BM03" -cell "OEQINVD4" -version IC251_ISR5-023_CAT -mode replace -manage unmanaged -genOnly 1 ( will create replay files and NO virtuoso will be run using the created replay file)

7.Results will be posted in summary.txt file in the following location after performance run is completed.
==>/user/virtuoso.catdm/USERS/CAT_DM/perfTest/result/ ( with unique id and build no eg:-   1775604261_IC25.1-64b.ISR5.EA.23 )
eg of summary.txt
---
Test7_BM01_managed_1775604261_IC25.1-64b.ISR5.EA.23.log
Test7_BM01. Performance Copy Hierarchy to Non-empty Library managed time <time in seconds>
---

8.For reviewing the replay of the performance log file for each performance test run will be placed under CDS_log.
/user/virtuoso.catdm/USERS/CAT_DM/perfTest/CDS_log

